{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/README.md --jq .content | base64 -d'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/README.md --jq .content | base64 -d'","aggregated_output":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card, longer if one asks for more time: what\n   the game is, how to win, the controls. The card is the hub's, from the\n   game's tags, or the game's own (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n### Tags\n\nIn the game's `<head>`:\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"MIN-MAX\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"MODE\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"GOAL\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"CONTROLS\">\n```\n\n- `hub:session-players`: the smallest and largest number of players the game\n  takes in a session. The hub deals the game only when the number of players\n  is in that range.\n- `hub:session-mode`: `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world`.\n- `hub:session-goal` and `hub:session-howto`: how to win and the game's\n  controls, shown on the hub's card.\n\nOptional:\n\n- `hub:session-minutes`: how many minutes a round of the game takes. The hub\n  shows it and uses it to decide when to call time.\n- `hub:webgpu` with `required`: the game cannot run without WebGPU. The hub\n  then deals it only when every player's browser has WebGPU.\n\n### The client\n\n[session.js](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js)\nis pasted into the game unmodified, as the first script in `<head>`, right\nafter `<meta charset>`. In a session it:\n\n- seeds `Math.random`, in parallel and ghost, before any of the game's own\n  scripts run, so it gives the same numbers on every copy;\n- gives the game an empty `localStorage` and `sessionStorage` of its own, so\n  nothing stored on the device carries into the round, and nothing the round\n  stores reaches the device's own storage;\n- hands `requestFullscreen()` and `exitFullscreen()` to the hub, which takes\n  its whole page fullscreen; `document.fullscreenElement` and\n  `fullscreenchange` follow the hub's page.\n\nThe hub replaces an unmodified copy of the client with each new version. An\nedited copy is not replaced.\n\n### Joining\n\n- `AIHub.active` is `true` from the first line when the hub opened the page.\n- In a session, the game opens straight into the round: no title screen,\n  menus or prompts before it, other than its own card (*The card*).\n- `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats: [min, max] })` returns a promise of the\n  round's `info`, or of `null` when there is no hub after all; with `null`\n  the game runs as it does on its own.\n- `AIHub.ready()` is called once, when the game has loaded and the round can\n  start, with no key press: the players answer the card.\n- The round starts when the card's countdown ends or every player pressed\n  Ready, and every game has called `ready()`. A game still loading then gets\n  20 more seconds; after that its player sits the round out.\n\n`info` (also on `AIHub` after `connect()`):\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `me` | this copy's player id |\n| `players` | `[{ id, name, color }]`, ids `0..N-1` in seat order |\n| `host`, `isHost` | the id of the copy that runs a shared world, and whether it is this one |\n| `server` | `true` only on a copy that hosts a shared world with no player of its own |\n| `mode`, `round`, `limitMs` | the mode, the round number, and the round's hard limit after the start |\n| `seed` | a number, the same on every copy, behind `AIHub.rng(label)` |\n\nNames come from the hub and are never inserted into the page as HTML. Colours\nfollow the seat: `#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`, `#f5b700`.\n\n### The card\n\nBefore every round the players get 10 to 30 seconds to learn what comes\nnext and say when they are ready. A player can ask for more time, which adds\nten seconds; while more than half of them are asking, the countdown holds.\nBy default the hub shows its own card over the game. A game can make the\ncard its own, as part of the game:\n\n```js\nAIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card: true });\n```\n\nThe hub's card then steps aside when the game calls `ready()`, and the game's\nscreen is the card until `start`. How it looks and sounds is the game's: its\ntitle, its music, its world, the players lining up. Introduce the game the way\nit deserves.\n\nWhile it is on, the card shows:\n\n- the game's name;\n- the players, each in their colour, and which of them are ready;\n- how to win the round;\n- the controls this player will use;\n- the time left, from the `card` event.\n\nAnd it takes two answers, from the keyboard, a controller, or a tap or click\non the card:\n\n- **Ready**: Enter, Cross (button 0), or a tap on Ready:\n  `AIHub.answer('ready')`.\n- **More time**: Triangle (button 3), a key the card names, or a tap on More\n  time: `AIHub.answer('more')`. Answering `more` again takes it back.\n\nNothing done on the card changes the round. It has no menus, settings or\nchoices, and play begins only at `start`. In parallel and ghost it draws no\nnumbers from `Math.random`, which would change the round's start: use\n`AIHub.rng('card')`.\n\n`card` arrives whenever it changes, and every second while the countdown runs:\n\n| Field | |\n|---|---|\n| `left` | milliseconds until the round starts by itself; `null` while paused or starting |\n| `paused` | `true` while most players asked for more time |\n| `starting` | `true` once the countdown is over or everyone is ready: `start` follows when every game has loaded |\n| `ready` | the ids of the players who are ready |\n| `asking` | how many players asked for more time (never who) |\n| `asked` | `true` when this player asked for more time |\n\n### The start\n\n`start` arrives when the round starts. Play begins three seconds later, when\n`AIHub.time()` reaches 0. `AIHub.time()` is the same timeline on every device,\ngive or take about 15 ms: negative during the countdown, `-Infinity` before\n`start`.\n\n### Reporting\n\n- `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`, in parallel and ghost: the player's\n  standing during the round. `score` is a number, higher is ahead; `label` is\n  text for the hub's scoreboard. The hub takes the latest about once a second.\n- `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })`, in parallel and\n  ghost, once, when the player's round is over. `time` is milliseconds of\n  `AIHub.time()`, lower wins; `score` is a number, higher wins.\n- `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won })`, in a shared world, called once,\n  by the host only:\n  - `standings`: arrays of player ids, best first; players in the same array\n    tie. It lists every player still in the round once; anyone left out is\n    placed last.\n  - `scores` (optional): `{ id: number }`, shown on the scoreboard.\n  - `won` (optional): `true` or `false` when the round is a team result.\n\n### Time-up and the end\n\n- The hub may call time while the round is still going. On `time-up`, the\n  game reports within `graceMs`: a `result()` in parallel and ghost, a\n  `finish()` from the host in a shared world. A shared world with no\n  `finish()` by then is void.\n- `end` is the last message of a round. After it, the game takes no input and\n  sends nothing, and its sound stops. The hub shows its results over the\n  game, then removes it.\n\n| `end` reason | |\n|---|---|\n| `finished` | the round counted; `standings` is the final order |\n| `void` | it didn't count (no result, a fatal error, skipped) |\n| `host-left` | the host of a shared world left |\n| `sat-out` | this player missed the ready deadline |\n| `session-ended` | the session closed |\n\n### Leaving\n\n- `leave` arrives with `{ id, reason }` when a player leaves: `left`,\n  `disconnected`, `not-ready` or `kicked`. It is final for the round.\n- A parallel or ghost round goes on whoever leaves, the host included.\n- A shared-world round is void when its host leaves, isn't ready, or has its\n  tab hidden for more than 20 seconds.\n- `AIHub.fail(message)`: the game cannot run in this browser. From the host\n  of a shared world it voids the round; from any other copy it counts as\n  that player leaving.\n\n### Scoring\n\n- Parallel and ghost: players with a `time` rank first, lowest first; then\n  the rest by `score`. A player with no result is ranked by their last\n  progress.\n- Shared world: the host's `standings`. With `won`, the results show a team\n  result instead of medals.\n- Each player gets one point for every player they beat.\n\n`result()` and `finish()` may also carry `stats` and `awards`, shown with the\nresults:\n\n- in `result()`: `stats` is `{ name: value }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ title, detail }]`, for this player;\n- in `finish()`: `stats` is `{ id: { name: value } }` and `awards` is\n  `[{ id, title, detail }]`, for each player.\n\nPlaces and points come only from the standings, `time` and `score`.\n\n---\n\n## Sending data between copies\n\n### Parallel\n\nThe copies send nothing to each other. `send()` is not used.\n\n### Ghost\n\nEach copy sends its own player's position and what the player is doing to\nthe other copies with `send()`. Each copy shows the other players' characters\nonly while they are in the same area of the game as its own player, and those\ncharacters do not affect its world. `Math.random` is seeded as in parallel.\n\n### Shared world\n\n- The host's copy (`AIHub.isHost`) runs the world. The other copies send the\n  host what their own player does, and show the world the host sends them.\n- The hub can run the host's copy with no player of its own: `AIHub.server`\n  is `true` and `AIHub.me` is not among `AIHub.players`. The host's copy runs\n  the world in that case too, with no local player, camera or input.\n- `Math.random` is not seeded. `AIHub.rng(label)` gives the same numbers on\n  every copy.\n\n### `send()` and `message`\n\n- `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` sends `data` to every other copy, or\n  to the one player `to`. It returns `false` when the message is dropped.\n- `AIHub.on('message', (data, from) => …)` receives it; `from` is the\n  sender's player id. A copy never receives its own messages. Messages sent\n  before another copy has loaded are queued for it.\n- `data` is JSON, at most 16 KB.\n- At most 20 messages a second leave each copy, with bursts up to 40; the\n  client drops the rest.\n- Reliable messages (the default) arrive in the order they were sent.\n  Messages sent with `reliable: false` may be lost or arrive out of order. An\n  unreliable message larger than about 1,200 bytes travels as several packets\n  and is lost whole if any of them is.\n\n---\n\n## Rules\n\nIn a session:\n\n- **Network only through the hub.** No WebSocket, WebRTC, or `fetch` to a\n  game server or public broker. Loading the game's own files is fine.\n- **No communication between players.** No chat, voice, emotes or custom\n  names. Names come from the hub.\n- **The page stays.** No `alert`, `confirm` or `prompt`; no `window.open`,\n  new tabs or navigating away. Quitting, restarting or returning to a title\n  screen does nothing; the hub starts and ends rounds.\n- **Create + Options is the hub's.** On a controller, holding the two\n  together opens the hub's corner bar; the game ignores Options while Create\n  is held.\n\nEverything on this page applies only in a session (`AIHub.active`). Outside\none, the game is not affected.\n\n---\n\n## Test it\n\nThe harness plays the hub: it loads the game 1–4 times on a simulated network\nand runs the checks the hub runs when a game joins the library. Serve it next\nto the game:\n\n```bash\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/bridge.js\ncurl -fsSO https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/round.js\npython3 -m http.server 8000\n```\n\nThen open `http://localhost:8000/harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=2&auto=1`.\nThe hub's own test also runs ghost and shared-world games with\n`&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, again with\n`&scenario=host-leave`, and shared worlds once more with\n`&players=2&scenario=server`.\n\nThe checklist fills in as it runs. **A game passes when\n`window.__hubCheck.pass` is true**; `document.body.dataset.complete` becomes\n`\"true\"` at the end. It checks:\n\n- the tags, `connect()`, `ready()` with no key press, and the start;\n- with the game's own card, that Enter answers Ready;\n- parallel and ghost: `Math.random` the same on every copy, and progress from\n  every copy; parallel sends nothing, ghost sends;\n- shared world: traffic both ways, and a round hosted by a copy with no\n  player of its own;\n- a player leaving, the host leaving, time-up, a valid result, and every copy\n  told the round ended;\n- no protocol problems, errors, dialogs, popups or sockets.\n\n**New round**, **Time up**, **Remove player** and **Hide host tab** run the\ncases by hand; clicking a player's frame gives it the keyboard and mouse.\n`&limit=` sets the round's length in seconds and `&seed=` fixes the seed. The\ngame is served from the harness's own origin.\n\nIn the AI Hub repository, `node scripts/hub-check.mjs <game>` runs the same\nchecks with Playwright, then opens the game outside a session to see it still\nruns there.\n\n---\n\n## Reference\n\n### Tags\n\n| Tag | |\n|---|---|\n| `hub:session` | `1`: this protocol |\n| `hub:session-players` | `MIN-MAX`: the number of players the game takes in a session |\n| `hub:session-mode` | `parallel`, `ghost` or `shared-world` |\n| `hub:session-goal` | how to win, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-howto` | the controls, shown on the hub's card |\n| `hub:session-minutes` | optional: how many minutes a round takes |\n| `hub:webgpu` | optional: `required` when the game cannot run without WebGPU |\n\n### API\n\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| `AIHub.active` | `true` in a session, from the first line |\n| `AIHub.connect({ mode, seats, card? })` | → `Promise<info \\| null>`; `null`: no hub. `card: true`: the game shows its own card |\n| `AIHub.ready()` | once, when the round can start |\n| `AIHub.answer('ready' \\| 'more')` | on the game's own card, before `start` |\n| `AIHub.time()` | milliseconds since play began: negative in the countdown, `-Infinity` before `start` |\n| `AIHub.on(event, fn)` | returns a function that removes the handler |\n| `AIHub.progress({ score, label })` | parallel and ghost |\n| `AIHub.result({ time \\| score, stats?, awards? })` | parallel and ghost, once |\n| `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores?, won?, stats?, awards? })` | shared world, the host, once |\n| `AIHub.send(data, { to, reliable })` | ghost and shared world |\n| `AIHub.rng(label)` | a generator of numbers in `[0, 1)`, the same on every copy, one stream per label |\n| `AIHub.seeded` | `true` when the client seeded `Math.random` |\n| `AIHub.fail(message)` | the game cannot run in this browser |\n\n`AIHub.probe()` and `AIHub.inspect()` exist for older games; the hub does not\nread them.\n\n| Event | Arguments |\n|---|---|\n| `card` | `{ left, paused, starting, ready, asking, asked }`, with the game's own card |\n| `start` | `{ in }`: milliseconds until play begins |\n| `message` | `data, from` |\n| `leave` | `{ id, reason }` |\n| `time-up` | `{ graceMs }` |\n| `end` | `{ reason, standings }` |\n\nEvents that arrive before a handler is attached are kept, and delivered in\norder when the first handler is attached. Fields and events a newer hub adds\nreach the game through the client unchanged.\n\n### Versions\n\nThis is protocol **1**, client **1.4.0**. Changes within version 1 only add:\ngames on older clients keep working. A change that would break a game becomes\nprotocol 2, with its own `hub:session` value.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/retrofit.md --jq .content | base64 -d'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'gh api repos/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/contents/lib/hub/retrofit.md --jq .content | base64 -d'","aggregated_output":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time, stats })` or `AIHub.result({ score, stats })` once.\n   `stats` holds up to six numbers the game already keeps that say how the\n   run went, each under a name of at most 16 characters, for example\n   `{ Coins: 42, 'Best combo': 7 }`; add no counting for it, and leave it out\n   if the game keeps none. In `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current\n   score and stats at once if the run is still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"The random title draw selected **Californium Games**. Each event will have its own rhythm: pump and launch in the half-pipe, carve through the surf pocket, then link ramp tricks on the BMX course. AI Hub sessions will use parallel score competition, alongside hotseat play and standalone online rooms.\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > Californium-Games-California-Games-gpt-6.1-sol-ultra-20261105-212540/main.js <<'EOF'\nimport * as THREE from 'three';\nimport RAPIER from 'https://esm.sh/@dimforge/rapier3d-compat@0.19.3';\nimport {createArt} from './art.js';\nimport {AudioSystem} from './audio.js';\nimport {FestivalNetwork} from './network.js';\n\nconst \"'$=id=>document.getElementById(id), TAU=Math.PI*2, clamp=(v,a,b)=>Math.max(a,Math.min(b,v));\nconst esc=s=>String(s).replace(/[&<>\"'\"']/g,c=>({'&':'&amp;','<':'&lt;','>':'&gt;','\\\"':'&quot;',\\\"'\\\":'&#39;'}[c]));\nconst EVENTS=[{id:'skate',name:'HALF-PIPE HEAT',short:'Half-pipe',tag:'Concrete. Courage. Questionable shorts.',goal:'Pump the bowl. Pop at the lip. Bring it home.',guide:[['MOVE','Build speed through the bowl. Hold down to pump.'],['POP','Jump near a high wall for the biggest air.'],['STYLE','Grab or flip in the air. Release to level out.']],gold:3500,silver:1800,bronze:650},{id:'surf',name:'SALTWATER SWING',short:'Surfing',tag:'The forecast calls for absolutely tubular.',goal:'Follow the golden pocket. Carve, pop, repeat.',guide:[['CARVE','Steer left and right to follow the golden wave pocket.'],['SCORE','Stay in the pocket to earn flow points. Grab for a cutback.'],['AIR','Pop off the wave, then grab or flip. Watch the red buoy.']],gold:4200,silver:2200,bronze:800},{id:'bmx',name:'BOARDWALK BMX',short:'BMX',tag:'Two wheels. Zero sensible decisions.',goal:'Pedal the ramps. Clear the cones. Land your style.',guide:[['PEDAL','Hold right to sprint. Left slows you down.'],['POP','Jump at the ramp lip; jump over orange cones.'],['STYLE','Tailwhip or barspin in the air. Release before landing.']],gold:3500,silver:1800,bronze:650}];\nconst DEFAULTS={speed:1,gravity:18,jump:8,assist:.78,duration:60,timeScale:1};\nlet config={...DEFAULTS},audio=new AudioSystem(),world,body,art,renderer,ready=false;\nlet state={screen:'loading',event:'skate',eventIndex:0,time:0,elapsed:0,airborne:false,speed:0,trick:'',crashed:false,total:0,score:0,pending:0,mult:1,rotation:0,combo:[],bestCombo:0,bails:0,landings:0,flow:0,started:false};\nlet currentPlayer=0,playerCount=1,players=[],practice=false,attract=false,lastInput=performance.now(),inputKind='keyboard',glyphs='ps',soundOn=true,reduceMotion=false,bot=false,infinite=false,hubInfo=null,hubEnded=false,hubResult=false,hubStarting=false,network=null,networkScores=[],onlineWaiting=false;\nlet eventElapsed=0,crashTime=0,lastGround=true,airTime=0,lastTrick=-9,dir=1,pipeSpeed=9,targetX=0,flowClock=0,foamClock=0,toastTime=0,scoreFlash=0,lastRender=0,lastNetwork=0,lookOffset=0;\nconst keys=new Set(),pressed=new Set(),padPrev=[],touch={active:false,x:0,y:0,startX:0,startY:0,moveX:0,moveY:0},stats={frames:0,physicsSteps:0,errors:[],bailReasons:[]};\nlet best={};try{best=JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('californium-best')||'{}')}catch{}\nfunction persist(){if(\"'!AIHub.active)try{localStorage.setItem('\"'californium-best',JSON.stringify(best))}catch{}}\nfunction isPlay(){return state.screen==='playing'||attract}\nfunction noteInput(kind='keyboard'){inputKind=kind;lastInput=performance.now();if(attract){attract=false;bot=false;showTitle();return true}updatePrompts();audio.unlock();return false}\nfunction label(action){const maps={keyboard:{pop:'SPACE',grab:'J',flip:'K',pause:'ESC',move:'A D / ← →',pump:'S / ↓',accept:'ENTER'},ps:{pop:'✕',grab:'□',flip:'○',pause:'OPTIONS',move:'L STICK',pump:'L STICK ↓',accept:'✕'},xbox:{pop:'A',grab:'X',flip:'B',pause:'MENU',move:'L STICK',pump:'L STICK ↓',accept:'A'},touch:{pop:'TAP',grab:'AUTO',flip:'AUTO',pause:'Ⅱ',move:'DRAG',pump:'ASSIST',accept:'TAP'}};return maps[inputKind==='gamepad'?glyphs:inputKind]?.[action]||action}\nfunction updatePrompts(){document.querySelectorAll('[data-key]').forEach(e=>e.textContent=label(e.dataset.key));document.body.dataset.input=inputKind;\"'$('\"'touch-pop').textContent='POP';}\nfunction toast(text,kind=''){ \"'$('\"'toast').textContent=text;\"'$('\"'toast').className='toast visible '+kind;toastTime=3; }\nfunction visiblePanel(id){document.querySelectorAll('.panel').forEach(e=>e.hidden=e.id\"'!==id);$('\"'overlay').hidden=\"'!id;$('\"'hud').hidden=\"'!isPlay();$('\"'attract').hidden=\"'!attract;focusFirst();}\nfunction focusFirst(){requestAnimationFrame(()=>{const a=[...document.querySelectorAll('\"'.panel:not([hidden]) button,.panel:not([hidden]) input')].find(e=>\"'!e.disabled);a?.focus({preventScroll:true})})}\nfunction setScreen(s,p){state.screen=s;visiblePanel(p);updatePrompts()}\nfunction showTitle(){state.screen='\"'title';attract=false;state.crashed=false;art?.setEvent('skate');state.event='skate';if(body){body.setTranslation({x:-2,y:1,z:0},true);body.setLinvel({x:0,y:0,z:0},true)}\"'$('\"'title-best').textContent=best.festival?\"'`PERSONAL BEST  ${best.festival.toLocaleString()}`:'\"'THREE EVENTS. ONE GOLDEN COAST.';setScreen('title','title-panel');lastInput=performance.now();}\nfunction makePlayers(){players=Array.from({length:playerCount},(_,i)=>({name:network?.connected?\"'`RIDER ${network.me+1}`:`RIDER ${i+1}`,scores:[0,0,0],total:0}));currentPlayer=0;}\nfunction beginFestival(single=-1){if(AIHub.active&&!hubStarting)return;practice=single>=0;makePlayers();state.eventIndex=single>=0?single:0;showBrief();}\nfunction showBrief(){const e=EVENTS[state.eventIndex];state.event=e.id;art.setEvent(e.id);$('\"'brief-num').textContent=\"'`${practice?'\"'FREE SESSION':\"'`EVENT ${state.eventIndex+1} / 3`}  ·  ${players[currentPlayer].name}`;$('\"'brief-title').textContent=e.name;\"'$('\"'brief-tag').textContent=e.tag;\"'$('\"'brief-goal').textContent=e.goal;\"'$('\"'brief-guide').innerHTML=e.guide.map(([a,b],i)=>\"'`<div class=\"guide-row\"><b>0${i+1}</b><div><strong>${a}</strong><p>${b}</p></div></div>`).join('\"'');\"'$('\"'brief-medals').textContent=\"'`BRONZE ${e.bronze}   /   SILVER ${e.silver}   /   GOLD ${e.gold}`;setScreen('\"'brief','brief-panel');}\nfunction height(x,id=state.event){if(id==='skate'){const a=Math.max(0,Math.abs(x)-4);return 4*(a/8)**2}if(id==='bmx'){for(const c of [-9,3,15])if(x>=c-3&&x<=c)return (x-(c-3))/3*2.2;return 0}return .4+.5*Math.sin(x*.22+state.elapsed*1.8)}\nfunction buildPhysics(){if(world)world.free();world=new RAPIER.World({x:0,y:-config.gravity,z:0});world.timestep=1/60;body=world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.dynamic().setTranslation(-5,3,0).lockRotations().enabledTranslations(true,true,false).setLinearDamping(.03).setCcdEnabled(true));world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.ball(.38).setFriction(.02).setRestitution(0),body);if(state.event\"'!=='\"'surf'){for(let x=-20;x<20;x+=.4){const h1=height(x),h2=height(x+.4),a=Math.atan2(h2-h1,.4),length=Math.hypot(.4,h2-h1);if(Math.abs(h2-h1)>1)continue;const ground=world.createRigidBody(RAPIER.RigidBodyDesc.fixed().setTranslation(x+.2,(h1+h2)/2-.12,0).setRotation({x:0,y:0,z:Math.sin(a/2),w:Math.cos(a/2)}));world.createCollider(RAPIER.ColliderDesc.cuboid(length/2,.12,4).setFriction(0),ground)}}}\nfunction startEvent(){eventElapsed=0;state.time=config.duration;state.elapsed=0;state.score=0;state.pending=0;state.mult=1;state.rotation=0;state.combo=[];state.trick='';state.crashed=false;state.airborne=false;state.flow=0;crashTime=0;pipeSpeed=9;dir=1;flowClock=0;foamClock=0;lastTrick=-9;airTime=0;lastGround=true;state.started=true;buildPhysics();const x=state.event==='skate'?-6:state.event==='bmx'?-17:0;body.setTranslation({x,y:height(x)+.42,z:0},true);body.setLinvel({x:0,y:0,z:0},true);art.setEvent(state.event);setScreen('playing',null);audio.resume();audio.voice('start');toast(state.event==='surf'?'CHASE THE GOLDEN POCKET':'GET RAD. LAND CLEAN.');}\nfunction medal(score,e=EVENTS[state.eventIndex]){return score>=e.gold?'GOLD':score>=e.silver?'SILVER':score>=e.bronze?'BRONZE':'SUN-SEEKER'}\nfunction bank(){if(\"'!state.pending)return;let pts=Math.round(state.pending*state.mult);state.score+=pts;state.bestCombo=Math.max(state.bestCombo,pts);state.landings++;toast(`${state.combo.join('\"' + ')}   +\"'${pts.toLocaleString()}`,'\"'good');audio.sfx('land');audio.sfx('score');if(pts>700)audio.voice('rad');state.pending=0;state.combo=[];state.mult=clamp(state.mult+1,1,8);scoreFlash=.4;publish();}\nfunction bail(reason){if(attract||bot||inputKind==='touch'){state.rotation=0;bank();return}state.bails++;state.pending=0;state.combo=[];state.mult=1;state.crashed=true;crashTime=1.25;state.rotation=0;stats.bailReasons.push(reason);toast(reason+' · BACK ON IN A BEAT','bad');audio.sfx('bail');audio.voice('bail');}\nfunction trick(kind){if(state.crashed||state.elapsed-lastTrick<.32)return;if(\"'!state.airborne){if(state.event==='\"'surf'&&kind==='grab'&&state.elapsed-lastTrick>1){lastTrick=state.elapsed;state.score+=90;toast('CUTBACK  +90');audio.sfx('score');publish()}return}lastTrick=state.elapsed;const name=state.event==='bmx'?(kind==='grab'?'TAILWHIP':'BARSPIN'):state.event==='surf'?(kind==='grab'?'MELON AIR':'REVERSE AIR'):(kind==='grab'?'METHOD GRAB':'KICKFLIP');const repeat=state.combo.includes(name);state.pending+=repeat?65:kind==='grab'?180:280;state.combo.push(name);state.trick=kind;state.rotation+=kind==='flip'?TAU:Math.PI*.18;audio.sfx('score');\"'$('\"'trick-call').textContent=name;scoreFlash=.3;}\nfunction jump(){if(\"'!lastGround||state.crashed)return;let v=body.linvel(),bonus=state.event==='\"'skate'?Math.max(0,(Math.abs(body.translation().x)-6)*.5):0;body.setLinvel({x:v.x,y:config.jump+bonus,z:0},true);body.setTranslation({x:body.translation().x,y:body.translation().y+.12,z:0},true);state.airborne=true;lastGround=false;airTime=0;audio.sfx('jump');}\nfunction publish(){const total=players[currentPlayer]?.total||0;const score=total+state.score;if(AIHub.active&&\"'!hubEnded&&!hubResult)AIHub.progress({score,label:`${EVENTS[state.eventIndex].short} · ${medal(state.score)}`});if(network?.connected)network.sendScore({event:state.eventIndex,score:state.score,total:score,finished:false});}\nfunction finishEvent(){bank();const p=players[currentPlayer],e=EVENTS[state.eventIndex];p.scores[state.eventIndex]=state.score;p.total=p.scores.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0);best[e.id]=Math.max(best[e.id]||0,state.score);persist();audio.sfx('\"'finish');\"'$('\"'result-eyebrow').textContent=\"'`${p.name}  /  ${e.short.toUpperCase()}`;$('\"'result-medal').textContent=medal(state.score);\"'$('\"'result-score').textContent=state.score.toLocaleString();\"'$('\"'result-copy').textContent=medal(state.score)==='GOLD'?'That coast is officially toast.':\"'`Next medal: ${state.score<e.bronze?e.bronze:state.score<e.silver?e.silver:e.gold} points. Keep the good times rolling.`;$('\"'result-detail').textContent=\"'`BEST COMBO ${state.bestCombo}  ·  CLEAN LANDINGS ${state.landings}  ·  WIPEOUTS ${state.bails}`;$('\"'result-next').textContent=practice?'RIDE AGAIN':currentPlayer+1<playerCount?'NEXT RIDER':state.eventIndex<2?'NEXT EVENT':'FESTIVAL RESULTS';setScreen('event-result','result-panel');if(attract){setTimeout(()=>{if(attract)advance()},1500)}else if(AIHub.active||network?.connected){setTimeout(()=>{if(state.screen==='event-result'&&\"'!hubEnded)advance()},3500)}}\nfunction advance(){if(practice){startEvent();return}if(currentPlayer+1<playerCount){currentPlayer++;showBrief()}else if(state.eventIndex<2){currentPlayer=0;state.eventIndex++;state.event=EVENTS[state.eventIndex].id;showBrief()}else{finishFestival();return}if(attract||AIHub.active||network?.connected)startEvent();}\nfunction finishFestival(){best.festival=Math.max(best.festival||0,...players.map(p=>p.total));persist();$('\"'podium-list').innerHTML=[...players].sort((a,b)=>b.total-a.total).map((p,i)=>\"'`<div class=\"standing\"><span>0${i+1}</span><strong>${esc(p.name)}</strong><b>${p.total.toLocaleString()}</b></div>`).join('\"'');\"'$('\"'festival-copy').textContent=players[0].total>=11000?'GOLDEN COAST LEGEND. Put that on a T-shirt.':'Three sports. One seriously excellent afternoon.';setScreen('festival-result','festival-panel');if(AIHub.active)reportHub();if(network?.connected)network.sendScore({event:2,score:state.score,total:players[0].total,finished:true});audio.voice('finish');if(attract)setTimeout(()=>{if(attract){state.eventIndex=0;currentPlayer=0;makePlayers();state.event='skate';startEvent()}},2500);}\nfunction reportHub(){if(hubResult||hubEnded)return;hubResult=true;AIHub.result({score:(players[0]?.total||0)+(isPlay()?state.score:0),stats:{'Best combo':state.bestCombo,'Clean landings':state.landings,Wipeouts:state.bails}})}\nfunction pause(){if(attract||hubEnded)return;if(state.screen==='playing'){setScreen('paused','pause-panel');audio.suspend()}else if(['paused','settings','dev','about'].includes(state.screen)&&state.started){setScreen('playing',null);audio.resume()}}\nlet returnScreen='title';function openPanel(name){returnScreen=state.screen;setScreen(name,name+'-panel')}\nfunction back(){if(state.screen==='playing'){pause();return}if(state.screen==='paused'){pause();return}if(['settings','about','dev','online','practice'].includes(state.screen)){if(returnScreen==='paused')setScreen('paused','pause-panel');else showTitle()}else if(\"'!AIHub.active&&!network?.running)showTitle()}\n\nwindow.addEventListener('\"'keydown',e=>{if(['ArrowUp','ArrowDown','ArrowLeft','ArrowRight','Space','Enter'].includes(e.code))e.preventDefault();if(noteInput())return;if(\"'!keys.has(e.code))pressed.add(e.code);keys.add(e.code);if(e.code==='\"'Escape'){back();return}if(\"'!isPlay()){if(e.code==='\"'ArrowDown'||e.code==='ArrowUp')navigate(e.code==='ArrowDown'?1:-1);if(e.code==='Enter'||e.code==='Space'){if(document.activeElement?.tagName==='BUTTON')document.activeElement.click()}}});\nwindow.addEventListener('keyup',e=>keys.delete(e.code));window.addEventListener('blur',()=>{keys.clear();pressed.clear();if(state.screen==='playing'&&\"'!AIHub.active&&!attract)pause()});\nwindow.addEventListener('\"'pointerdown',e=>{if(e.pointerType\"'!=='\"'touch')noteInput('keyboard')});document.addEventListener('pointerover',e=>{if(e.target.matches('button'))e.target.focus({preventScroll:true})});\n\"'$('\"'view').addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{if(e.pointerType==='mouse'&&isPlay())lookOffset=(e.clientX/innerWidth-.5)*2;});\n\"'$('\"'view').addEventListener('pointerdown',e=>{if(e.pointerType==='touch'){if(noteInput('touch'))return;touch.active=true;touch.startX=e.clientX;touch.startY=e.clientY;touch.x=e.clientX;touch.y=e.clientY;touch.moveX=0;touch.moveY=0;touch.startTime=performance.now();e.target.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId)}else if(isPlay()){pressed.add(e.button===2?'KeyJ':'Space')}});\n\"'$('\"'view').addEventListener('contextmenu',e=>e.preventDefault());\"'$('\"'view').addEventListener('pointermove',e=>{if(e.pointerType==='touch'&&touch.active){touch.moveX=clamp((e.clientX-touch.startX)/65,-1,1);touch.moveY=clamp((e.clientY-touch.startY)/65,-1,1)}});\"'$('\"'view').addEventListener('pointerup',e=>{if(e.pointerType==='touch'){if(performance.now()-touch.startTime<250)pressed.add('Space');touch.active=false;touch.moveX=touch.moveY=0}});\nfunction navigate(d){const els=[...document.querySelectorAll('.panel:not([hidden]) button,.panel:not([hidden]) input')].filter(e=>\"'!e.disabled);let i=els.indexOf(document.activeElement);els[(i+d+els.length)%els.length]?.focus({preventScroll:true});audio.sfx('\"'click');}\nfunction readPad(){const pad=[...navigator.getGamepads()].find(p=>p?.connected);if(\"'!pad)return{x:0,y:0};const axis=Math.abs(pad.axes[0]||0)>.18?pad.axes[0]:0,ay=Math.abs(pad.axes[1]||0)>.18?pad.axes[1]:0;const edges=pad.buttons.map((b,i)=>b.pressed&&!padPrev[i]);const any=edges.some(Boolean)||Math.abs(axis)>.2||Math.abs(ay)>.2;if(any){if(inputKind!=='\"'gamepad'||edges.some(Boolean)){if(noteInput('gamepad')){pad.buttons.forEach((b,i)=>padPrev[i]=b.pressed);return{x:0,y:0}}}if(edges[9]&&\"'!pad.buttons[8]?.pressed)pause();if(isPlay()){if(edges[0])pressed.add('\"'Space');if(edges[2])pressed.add('KeyJ');if(edges[1])pressed.add('KeyK')}else{if(edges[12])navigate(-1);if(edges[13])navigate(1);if(edges[0])document.activeElement?.click();if(edges[1])back();if((edges[14]||edges[15])&&document.activeElement?.type==='range'){const el=document.activeElement;el.value=+el.value+(edges[15]?1:-1)*+el.step;el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'))}}pad.buttons.forEach((b,i)=>padPrev[i]=b.pressed);return{x:axis,y:ay}}\nfunction controls(pad){let x=clamp((keys.has('KeyD')||keys.has('ArrowRight')?1:0)-(keys.has('KeyA')||keys.has('ArrowLeft')?1:0)+pad.x+touch.moveX,-1,1),y=clamp((keys.has('KeyS')||keys.has('ArrowDown')?1:0)-(keys.has('KeyW')||keys.has('ArrowUp')?1:0)+pad.y+touch.moveY,-1,1);if(bot||attract){const p=body.translation();x=state.event==='surf'?clamp((targetX-p.x)*.65,-1,1):state.event==='bmx'?1:dir;y=1;if(lastGround&&(state.event==='skate'?Math.abs(p.x)>8:state.event==='bmx'?[-9,3,15].some(c=>p.x>c-.8&&p.x<c+.5):state.elapsed%3<.08))pressed.add('Space');if(state.airborne&&airTime>.18&&airTime<.5)pressed.add('KeyJ');if(state.airborne&&airTime>.55&&airTime<.8)pressed.add('KeyK')}if(inputKind==='touch'&&state.airborne&&airTime>.2&&airTime<.3)pressed.add('KeyJ');return{x,y}}\nfunction step(dt,pad){if(hubEnded)return;if(state.crashed){crashTime-=dt;if(crashTime<=0){state.crashed=false;const p=body.translation();body.setTranslation({x:clamp(p.x,-11,11),y:height(clamp(p.x,-11,11))+.42,z:0},true);body.setLinvel({x:0,y:0,z:0},true);pipeSpeed=8;lastGround=true}return}state.elapsed+=dt;eventElapsed+=dt;if(\"'!infinite)state.time-=dt;if(state.time<=0){finishEvent();return}const c=controls(pad);let p=body.translation(),v=body.linvel();if(pressed.has('\"'Space'))jump();if(pressed.has('KeyJ'))trick('grab');if(pressed.has('KeyK'))trick('flip');v=body.linvel();let vx=v.x;\nif(state.event==='skate'){if(p.x>12.3&&v.y<0)dir=-1;if(p.x< -12.3&&v.y<0)dir=1;const slope=Math.sign(p.x)*Math.max(0,Math.abs(p.x)-4)/8;pipeSpeed=clamp(pipeSpeed+(c.y>.3?2.7:0)*dt-(Math.sign(vx)*slope*10)*dt,6,16);if(Math.abs(p.x)<8&&Math.abs(c.x)>.3)dir=Math.sign(c.x);vx=dir*pipeSpeed*con